data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrclcap — mission report\\n\\n## Mission\\nDeliver src/greet.py with greet(name) returning \\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\" and\\ntests/test_greet.py covering a normal name and the empty string, with\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nAll three criteria are satisfied, verified independently by the orchestrator\\nagainst dev's committed branch (not merely by trusting dev's report).\\n\\n## Work performed\\n\\n1. Confirmed dev's briefing readback (dispatch d001) and accepted it.\\n2. Dispatched the mission (d002) to dev with the exact requirements.\\n3. dev implemented:\\n   - `src/greet.py`: `def greet(name): return f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`\\n   - `tests/test_greet.py`: unittest `TestCase` with `test_normal_name`\\n     (`greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`) and `test_empty_string`\\n     (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n   - Committed as `4f98c0f2d1795f77edcb8fd985d7b9d63baea2bc` (\\\"Add greet\\n     function with unittest coverage\\\") on dev's branch\\n     `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`.\\n4. Orchestrator verification: fetched `refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`,\\n   inspected both file contents directly via `git show`, checked out the\\n   exact commit in an isolated worktree, and ran\\n   `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself — result: 2 tests, OK,\\n   exit code 0.\\n5. Accepted d002.\\n\\n## Branches\\n- Orchestrator branch `cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`:\\n  no source changes of its own (orchestrator writes no code per its brief);\\n  contains only this run's coordination activity.\\n- dev branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`: carries the\\n  mission deliverable at commit `4f98c0f2d1795f77edcb8fd985d7b9d63baea2bc`.\\n\\n## Unmet items\\nNone.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

